\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S5}{\ignorespaces Headline degradation study (RQ1), \textbf  {synthetic effect model} ($M{=}738$, $\epsilon {=}\alpha {=}0.05$, seed-locked). $\mathrm  {ASR}_{\mathrm  {act}}^{\dagger }\downarrow $ / $\mathrm  {NRP}_{\mathrm  {sys}}^{\dagger }\uparrow $ are better. Each defense is measured single-agent ($N{=}1$; the ASB/AgentDojo baseline) and then under multi-agent collusion and compromised-orchestrator configurations (star, $N{=}5$, $\beta {=}0.3$). The guardrail's relative $\mathrm  {ASR}_{\mathrm  {act}}^{\dagger }$ reduction over no-defense is $41.6\%\to 31.8\%\to 27.6\%$ left to right; the $\dagger $ marks the \emph  {single-agent} predicate, so these columns are not the system metric, and the shrinkage between them is not statistically resolved at this budget (\Cref  {app:power}).}}{8}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:degradation}{{S5}{8}{Headline degradation study (RQ1), \textbf {synthetic effect model} ($M{=}738$, $\epsilon {=}\alpha {=}0.05$, seed-locked). $\ASRa ^{\dagger }\downarrow $ / $\NRPs ^{\dagger }\uparrow $ are better. Each defense is measured single-agent ($N{=}1$; the ASB/AgentDojo baseline) and then under multi-agent collusion and compromised-orchestrator configurations (star, $N{=}5$, $\betafrac {=}0.3$). The guardrail's relative $\ASRa ^{\dagger }$ reduction over no-defense is $41.6\%\to 31.8\%\to 27.6\%$ left to right; the $\dagger $ marks the \emph {single-agent} predicate, so these columns are not the system metric, and the shrinkage between them is not statistically resolved at this budget (\Cref {app:power})}{table.caption.10}{}}
